From 38a8d3de57d8eb344da30919c80cf365136638e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:25:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban operator: refuse an unproven caller before
 deferring it; '--'/U+2212 dashes; be/being govern

Review t_01a1d4254843641b (PR #2037 @051fdf9621, GitHub review 5888574999).

Blocking: apply_incoming ran home_refusal before _caller_refusal, so a forged
call whose caller has no created event in the replica was deferred before its
caller was proven. With a future requested_at (payload-supplied, no clock
check) it was retried every tick, never refused, and the held watermark paged
the whole request tail each tick. Now the replica-only caller checks
(_caller_replica_refusal, split out of _caller_refusal; no Board read) run
first: an unproven caller is refused, never deferred. A requested_at more than
SKEW_S in the future is caller_unproven, and home_refusal defers only within
[-CREATION_SYNC_SKEW_S, CREATION_SYNC_GRACE_S] of now (defence in depth).
The filter and the home check move into _incoming/_home_check (apply_incoming
CC stays under target).

Nits: a spaced ASCII '--' and U+2212 are dash boundaries ("Not done -- posted
to t_X" is a claim); "be"/"being" join _NOT_CLAIM, so "to be later posted",
"to be eventually sent" and "is being posted" are not claims; the guard
comment notes the accepted fail-open "turned out to be posted twice".

Proof: RED on 051fdf9621: 7 new cases fail (forged unproven caller at now and
at now+3600 deferred instead of refused, home_refusal future defer, 5
classifier cases). GREEN: 7 operator/consent test files, 325 passed. Mutant
(home_refusal without the replica-first gate) killed by the now-offset case.
